<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roger of Lauria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1245–1305</span> · Also known as Ruggero di Lauria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roger of Lauria was an admiral in the service of the Crown of Aragon and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, regarded as one of the greatest naval commanders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicilian-vespers">War of the Sicilian Vespers</a> he won a series of victories over the Angevin fleets, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-naples">Gulf of Naples</a> in 1284. In the same year he seized the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djerba">Jerba</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafsid-dynasty">Hafsids</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roger-of-lauria.jpg" alt="Roger of Lauria" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thom Quine · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roger_de_Ll%C3%BAria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
